TY  - JOUR
DB  - APA PsycInfo <2023 to December Week 2 2023>
ID  - 2024-12019-287
T1  - Voices of Latinx parents: Perceptions of engagement in middle school student education amidst the COVID 19 pandemic.
T3  - Dissertation Abstracts International
A1  - Schisler, Amanda
Y1  - 2024//
N2  - This study explored the impact of COVID-19 on Latinx parent engagement in their middle school children's education. Through qualitative narrative inquiry, an examination of challenges and opportunities arising from the pandemic-related shift to remote learning were shared. The data identified that while some Latinx parents faced challenges relating to the adaptation of remote learning, limited access to technology, and engaging with their children's education, others found ways to become more involved and built stronger relationships with their children's teachers. Recommendations for improving Latinx parent engagement in middle school children's education in the context of both in-person and virtual learning were identified. (PsycInfo Database Record (c) 2023 APA, all rights reserved)
