350. 
TY  - JOUR
DB  - APA PsycInfo <2023 to December Week 2 2023>
ID  - 2023-85470-144
T1  - The effects of music mood and binaural beats on academic advertising.
T3  - Dissertation Abstracts International
A1  - Omeroglu, Fatih Baha
Y1  - 2023//
N2  - How music affects our mood, cognition, and feelings have been studied over the years. Since the effect of music on mood and cognition has been demonstrated many times, various implications adopted use of music heavily. In recent years, use of music has been doubled and currently 86% of advertising uses some sort of musical stimuli alongside of their advertised content and product. Effect of music in advertising has been studied in many different ways, and our study specifically analyzes the effect of music mood in advertising with two phases. The initial phase is conducted online through YouTube to see if music mood makes any difference in viewers engagement to the academic commercial. The second phase of the study is conducted in a lab setting where it incorporated more biometric measures to improve research even further with the use of electroencephalography (EEG) and eye tracking. Additionally, this phase of the study has also introduced a new concept and idea of binaural beat usage in advertising setting. The goal of this research is to identify effect of music mood and binaural beats in advertising using scientific methodologies with biometrics measures such as EEG brain waves and pupil dilations with eye tracking. Findings of this research can serve as a valuable guideline for future marketing implications, especially in academic advertising. (PsycInfo Database Record (c) 2023 APA, all rights reserved)
