399. 
TY  - JOUR
DB  - APA PsycInfo <2023 to December Week 2 2023>
ID  - 2023-85468-250
T1  - Medicaid strategies to maintain access to maternity care in rural America.
T3  - Dissertation Abstracts International
A1  - Cochran-McClain, Caroline
Y1  - 2023//
N2  - Providing access to maternity care in rural areas is a growing concern. An estimated half a million rural women give birth in US hospitals each year, the majority of whom deliver at their community hospitals and therefore rely on local maternity services. Recent closures of rural obstetric units and entire hospitals have exacerbated challenges with access to care for more than twenty-eight million women of reproductive age living in rural America, many of whom are covered by Medicaid. This study uses an exploratory qualitative design to provide a descriptive analysis of how Medicaid policy can facilitate local access to maternity services for rural women, focusing on the Medicaid-related factors, strategy to support those factors, and replicability of those strategies. The research employed a sequential information-gathering strategy involving document review and key informant interviews with experts in the field. Overall, the study identifies a cadre of strategies the federal government and state Medicaid programs can adopt that address access through policy mechanisms related to workforce, payment models, program elements, and regional service delivery. (PsycInfo Database Record (c) 2023 APA, all rights reserved)
