511. 
TY  - JOUR
DB  - APA PsycInfo <2023 to December Week 2 2023>
ID  - 2023-68886-241
T1  - Latino counselor experience of working with other Latinos and substance abuse.
T3  - Dissertation Abstracts International
A1  - Santiago, Andrea
Y1  - 2023//
N2  - This study focuses on understanding the experiences of Latin substance abuse counselors working with clients of their own culture. Treatment in the United States is standard and previous research has shown minimal participation of Latinos in treatment. The research topic for this study is to explore the experiences of Latin substance abuse counselors working with clients of their own culture. This research will advance psychology by expanding prior research within the Latino community; it will help Latino communities and substance abuse professionals identify alternative options to become culturally competent in dealing with abuse issues. The study is qualitative, as counselor experiences will be used, and a generic design since the topic includes individual perceptions and experiences. Eight counselors from Latino countries working in the substance abuse field with experience with Latinos and substance abuse will voluntarily agree to participate in the study. Data analysis was completed using the generic design since the research question is specific to the counselor's personal experiences with the topic. Once the data analysis was conducted, seven patterns were identified, including the lack of services for Latinos, the language barrier, having a family as support, the need for community support to recover from substance use, considering the Latino religious values and faith to help with the recovery process, the use of motivational interviewing to address Latino clients, and finally prejudice as a risk factor to use. Most participants agreed that the main limitations for Latinos are the lack of services and the language barrier, which corresponds with the literature review completed for the study.  (PsycInfo Database Record (c) 2023 APA, all rights reserved)
