528. 
TY  - JOUR
DB  - APA PsycInfo <2023 to December Week 2 2023>
ID  - 2023-38658-214
T1  - Human resource professionals' perceptions of the influence of servant leadership style on employee engagement.
T3  - Dissertation Abstracts International
A1  - Taylor, Halima
Y1  - 2023//
N2  - The purpose of this study was to examine human resource professionals' perceptions of the influence of servant leadership style on employee engagement. Organizations utilize strategies and best practices to enhance employee workplace conditions. Leadership style has been examined as an influential component of employee engagement. Additional studies are needed that focus on the influence of servant leadership on employee engagement. The study used a generic qualitative research design. Thirteen human resource professionals participated in the study. Semi-structured interviews were executed with each participant. The collected data was analyzed using open, axial, and selective coding. The findings in this study revealed that servant leadership style influences employee engagement. The four themes which emerged include communication, awareness, support, and culture. Additional research may be needed to include different industries and assess the differences between human resource professionals' experiences based on their tenure. (PsycInfo Database Record (c) 2023 APA, all rights reserved)
