M1  - A clarification is necessary here. The goal usually discussed in the literature on financial COI disclosure is the promotion of trust simpliciter, rather than of warranted trust. But, in general, promoting trust simpliciter is not a worthy moral goal. Trusting those who ought not to be trusted or trusting them for the wrong reasons is not something that ought to be encouraged. Indeed, as I discuss below, this clarification is very important when trying to determine the effects of conflict disclosure on trust.
