ID  - 2022-45976-026
DO  - https://dx.doi.org/10.1093/ntr/ntab219
T1  - Bayesian inference: Evaluating replication attempts with Bayes factors.
A1  - Baig, Sabeeh A
AI  - Baig, Sabeeh A.; ORCID: https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1482-7127
A2  - Baig, S. A., Byron, M. J., Boynton, M. H., Brewer, N. T., Ribisl, K. M., Baig, S. A., Bollen, K. A., Harden, J. J., Ray, S., Zavisca, J., Gelman, A., Lee, D., Guo, J., Harms, C., Jarosz, A. F., Wiley, J., Jeon, M., De Boeck, P., Kary, A., Taylor, R., Donkin, C., Ly, A., Etz, A., Marsman, M., Wagenmakers, E. J., Marsman, M., Schonbrodt, F. D., Morey, R. D., Yao, Y., Gelman, A., Wagenmakers, E. J., Morey, R. D., Rouder, J. N., Jamil, T., Morey, M. R. D., Rouder, J. N., Engelhardt, C. R., McCabe, S., Morey, R. D., Rouder, J. N., Morey, R. D., Verhagen, J., Swagman, A. R., Wagenmakers, E. J., Team, R. C., Verhagen, J., Wagenmakers, E. J., Wu, H., Fai Cheung, S., On Leung, S., Zwaan, R. A., Etz, A., Lucas, R. E., Donnellan, M. B.
Y1  - 2022//
N2  - The second half of the previous decade saw a renewed focus in the research community on the reproducibility of scientific findings especially within social psychology and the behavioral sciences more generally. This renewed focus on scientific reproducibility has spurred the development of novel statistical methods to test replication success from two or more experiments. These methods have been formulated usually within a Bayesian framework that relies on Bayes factors and less so within likelihood-based or frequentist frameworks. Bayesian updating yields two general approaches for constructing Bayes factor tests of replication success: parameter updating and evidence updating. In this commentary, the author reviews both approaches for constructing replication Bayes factors for completeness and then describes in detail the evidence-updating approach with a focus on experimental research. This commentary concludes with an empirical application of evidence-updating replication Bayes factors to test replication success using simulated data from a published study of tobacco risk communication strategies. (PsycInfo Database Record (c) 2023 APA, all rights reserved)
