683. 
TY  - JOUR
DB  - APA PsycInfo <2023 to December Week 2 2023>
ID  - 2023-33086-062
T1  - Teacher perception of organizational culture after a leadership change in an educational organization.
T3  - Dissertation Abstracts International
A1  - Stone, LaDonna Roberta
Y1  - 2023//
N2  - The purpose of this qualitative case study was to explore how K-8 teachers perceive organizational culture after a change in principal leadership in one school district in Southern Virginia. This research study was guided by the three levels of culture theory. There were three research questions used in this study: RQ1: How do K-8 teachers perceive the physical artifacts aspect of organizational culture after a change in principal leadership in an educational organization? RQ2: How do K-8 teachers perceive the espoused values aspect of organizational culture after a change in principal leadership in an educational organization? RQ3: How do K-8 teachers perceive the underlying assumptions aspect of organizational culture after a change in principal leadership in an educational organization? Eleven K-8 teachers participated in the study. The three data sources used in the study were semi-structured interviews, a focus group, and artifact analysis of policies and procedures. Five themes derived from thematic analysis, artifact analysis, and study findings. The themes highlighted what 'mattered most' to teachers after a change in principal leadership to include differences in teacher behavior. The results indicated that teachers perceived their principal to value collaboration, student, and teacher well-being, and were more visible in schools that were described as having a strong school culture. This was described as fostering an 'emotional culture.' In schools that were described as having a poor or disjointed school culture perceived their principal to have poor communication skills and lacked involvement with teachers, students, and parents. Keywords: Organizational culture, principal leadership, three levels of culture, school culture. (PsycInfo Database Record (c) 2023 APA, all rights reserved)
