A2  - Bowles, W., Buck, J., Brinkman, B., Hixon, B., Guo, J., Zehala, A., Dawes, M., Summerskill, W., Glasziou, P., Cartabellotta, A., Martin, J., Hopayian, K., Porzsolt, F., Burls, A., Osborne, J., Larsen, C. M., Terkelsen, A. S., Kristensen, H. K., Carlsen, A.-M.- F., Majid, S., Foo, S., Luyt, B., Zhang, X., Theng, Y.-L., Chang, Y.-K., Mokhtar, I. A., Patelarou, A. E., Mechili, E. A., Ruzafa-Martinez, M., Dolezel, J., Gotlib, J., Skela-Savic, B., Ramos-Morcillo, A. J., Finotto, S., Jarosova, D., Smodis, M., Mecugni, D., Panczyk, M., Patelarou, E., World Health Organization
Y1  - 2023//
N2  - Comments on an article by Wendy Bowles et al. (see record 2021-21381-001). This international publication in the Journal of Clinical Nursing demonstrates the interest of this topic for nursing educators and nursing students worldwide. From the first Sicily Statement to the latest World Health Organization recommendations. Bowles et al. suggest that a partnership between clinical teams and university teachers in tutoring nursing students should be established to develop a culture of EBP for both students and practising nurses. The aim of their study was to compare the ECAP model with traditional clinical education in order to examine the effects of this strategy on student nurses and staff nurses. It is unfortunate, however, that the authors in the article do not argue the choice of the ECAP model. The authors wanted to promote the international replicability of this study. However, more information would be needed to achieve this objective. Indeed, this model starts with a hybrid version of a dedicated education unit (first part of the ECAP model) which is only described on the part carried out in the care units, without information on the teaching carried out at the university for the students. Two points need to be clarified concerning the study's data collection. Concerning the quantitative aspect, the sample of nurses is very small (8 out of 30), which makes the data unusable. (PsycInfo Database Record (c) 2023 APA, all rights reserved)
