757. 
TY  - JOUR
DB  - APA PsycInfo <2023 to December Week 2 2023>
ID  - 2023-21920-180
T1  - The influence of organizational culture on organizational innovation for employees in pharmaceutical organizations.
T3  - Dissertation Abstracts International
A1  - Shah, Janki
Y1  - 2023//
N2  - This research aimed to explore the extent to which organizational culture impacts organizational innovation for people working in pharmaceutical companies in the United States. Prior research showed that organizational culture is linked to organizational innovation. However, organizational culture has different typologies, such as clan culture, adhocracy culture, market culture, and hierarchy culture, each impacting organizational innovation differently. There was a gap in the literature about how each organizational culture typology affects innovation. This study used quantitative methodology to check the effect of each organizational culture type on organizational innovation. Since there were four typologies of organizational culture, which are independent variables, multiple regression was used. Ninety participants answered the survey questionnaire through the Question Pro platform based on the G*Power sample calculation and inclusion and exclusion criteria. The researcher used two instruments in the survey, the Organizational Culture Assessment Instrument (OCAI) to identify the organizational culture and the Organizational Innovativeness Assessment (OIA) for organizational innovation. The researcher transferred the completed survey responses to the Statistical Package for Social Sciences (SPSS) and conducted all the statistical analyses, such as descriptive statistics, correlation, tests of assumptions, model summary, Analysis of Variance (ANOVA), and collinearity diagnostics. The results showed that adhocracy culture results in a greater significant extent F(1,88) = 82.086, p < 0.001 of organizational innovation than the clan (F(1,88) = 55.952, p < 0.001), market (F(1,88) = 34.959, p < 0.001), and hierarchy (F(1,88) = 25.939, p < 0.001) cultures, respectively. Future researchers are recommended to check the effect of each typology of organizational culture with each different type of innovation to see the impact of which organizational culture results in which type of innovation. (PsycInfo Database Record (c) 2023 APA, all rights reserved)
