870. 
TY  - JOUR
DB  - APA PsycInfo <2023 to December Week 2 2023>
ID  - 2022-90099-034
T1  - Shared identity in marriage.
T3  - Dissertation Abstracts International
A1  - Richey, Angela M
Y1  - 2023//
N2  - This research presents a critical review of literature on shared identity formation in marriage and as an emerging concept for marital flourishing. Marriage has played a central role as a fundamental institution globally from the beginning of time. Individuals seek to merge lives, cultures, identities, and goals to form interdependence and a shared mission. However, unresolved challenges, increased expectations, and individualism can lead to conflict, disruption, and divorce, damaging the family and society. This body of work examines the background information on the state of marriage and reviews theoretical and empirical studies on shared identity and how it is formed, applied, and experienced. This review highlights the importance, benefits, and practices of shared identity in marriage with implications for couples, clergy, clinicians, coaches, and researchers. (PsycInfo Database Record (c) 2022 APA, all rights reserved)
