A3  - Storch, Eric A [Ed], Abramowitz, Jonathan S [Ed], McKay, Dean [Ed]
Y1  - 2022//
N2  - A variety of innovative technologies are available to support the delivery of exposure and response prevention (ERP) for obsessive-compulsive disorder (OCD), including mobile apps, web programs, and video telehealth delivery of psychotherapy. Although randomized controlled trials comparing ERP delivered via video telehealth to in-person delivery of ERP are lacking, preliminary effectiveness data from open trials and clinical cases suggest that technology can be feasibly and effectively integrated into evidence-based psychotherapy for OCD. Access to ERP for the treatment of OCD continues to be challenging for many individuals around the world, particularly those living in rural and underserved areas. Innovative technological solutions including mobile applications, internet-based programs, and video telehealth have the potential to expand access to mental health care for OCD. This chapter covers the use of technology in delivering ERP for OCD. It provides an overview of the various technology-based solutions that exist and the supporting evidence for each. As video telehealth delivery is the most commonly used and has the most empirical support, the chapter discusses the benefits and challenges of video telehealth delivery of ERP, discusses clinical, ethical, and legal considerations in the delivery of ERP via video telehealth, and reviews two case studies illustrating relevant issues. (PsycInfo Database Record (c) 2023 APA, all rights reserved)
