907. 
TY  - JOUR
DB  - APA PsycInfo <2022>
ID  - 2021-80518-097
T1  - A study to evaluate the quality of the homelessness management system in the Nevada plan to end youth homelessness.
T3  - Dissertation Abstracts International
A1  - Henderson, Aishia T
Y1  - 2022//
N2  - The purpose of this action research study was to evaluate the quality of the Homeless Management Information System (HMIS) with respect to reporting the incidence and prevalence of unaccompanied homeless youth in the Nevada region and consider if the HMIS data on unaccompanied homeless youth in the Nevada region is complete. Currently, HMIS is not used as the only data collection system to collect data on unaccompanied homeless youth by homeless youth service providers within the Nevada Homeless Continuum of Care (NH-CoC). The incomplete use of HMIS among homeless youth service providers creates inconsistent data on unaccompanied homeless youth and the true magnitude of youth homelessness in Nevada is unknown. This research study was an evaluation of HMIS within the context of the Nevada Plan to End Youth Homelessness to learn what key elements are needed to improve HMIS data quality, how HMIS data are used, and how data sharing in HMIS can help homeless youth providers better understand the needs of unaccompanied homeless youth in Nevada by performing qualitative interviews with homeless youth providers either use or do not use HMIS as their data collection system. The research design used in depth; audio recorded interviews that contained structured interview discussion guides with open ended questions. The study findings suggest that the following three areas will need to be addressed: (a) agency agreement on data sharing, (b) identify a new process that protects confidentiality, and (c) sharing progress notes without bias. (PsycInfo Database Record (c) 2023 APA, all rights reserved)
